</section>
</section>
<section id="S7" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">7 </span>Conclusion</h2>

<div id="S7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This paper presents a predictor-based LLM routing framework with cross-attention similarity module to optimize cost-performance trade-offs in multi-model environments. By modeling query-model interactions and introducing an exponential reward formulation, our method delivers robust and scalable routing across LLM pools. Empirical results on RouterBench confirm that attention-based predictors outperform traditional baselines in both efficiency and quality, achieving competitive AIQ scores and strong generalization across domains and tasks. These findings highlight the effectiveness of attention-driven routing for large-scale LLM deployment, offering a practical solution for balancing computational cost and response quality in dynamic, real-world settings.</p>
</div>
</section>
